# One full-resolution (1600x1200) mono frame, PNG-encoded on demand.
#
# The camera node retains the newest captured frame and encodes it only when
# asked: a 1600x1200 PNG costs tens of milliseconds, a quarter of the 10 Hz
# stream's budget, and nothing wants it most of the time. Calibration and
# single-shot diagnostics want it; the pose pipeline never does -- it consumes
# the 640x480 stream on `image`, where its own downscale is the identity.

# Refuse a frame older than this, in seconds. 0 accepts whatever is retained.
# A camera that died 30 s ago still has a retained frame, and calibrating on it
# would be silent nonsense, so the client states how fresh it needs the frame.
float32 max_age
---
bool success
string message
builtin_interfaces/Time capture_stamp
sensor_msgs/CompressedImage image
